## READ THESE FIRST (in this order)

1. **@docs/design-system/nexcyber-design-tokens.json** — Source of truth: every token (color, spacing, typography, motion, component styles) with dark/light variants and llmImplementationNotes. Reference this to understand token structure and constraints.
2. **@docs/design-system/nexcyber-design-system.md** — Detailed guide: token usage locations, card catalog, spacing scale, typography scale, theme behavior, mobile breakpoints, checklist. This is where all visual decisions are documented.
3. **@Nexcybers Color Palette.md** — Exact hex/rgba values for each color variable in dark and light themes. Verification reference only.
4. **@docs/Nueva sección - guía de estructura.md** — Page skeleton: header/footer, hero, celeste/theme band system, component library by section.
5. **@docs/design-system/guides/** — Content guides:
   - `blog-content.md` — How to add blog content
   - `resources-content.md` — How to add resources
   - `services-content.md` — How to add services
   (All without touching HTML/CSS)

This is a static multi-page site (`about.html`, `services.html`, `resources.html`, `blog.html`, `product.html`, `contact.html`, etc.) built with plain HTML + CSS + vanilla JS. No build step, no framework, no JSX.

## Mandatory flow before ANY visual change

**STEP 1 — Read the design guides** (no shortcuts, no guessing):
- nexcyber-design-tokens.json (understand token structure)
- nexcyber-design-system.md (§ references below point to sections here)

**STEP 2 — Understand core rules** before writing any CSS:
- **Spacing/sizing scale:** 4px multiples ONLY (4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 32…). NEVER 14px, 18px, 22px, or other odd values—they break the system. Exceptions: font-size uses clamp() for fluid scaling; border-radius follows 4px scale except buttons (100px pill, 0 on hover).
- **Colors via CSS variables ALWAYS:** `var(--token)` not hardcoded hex. ONLY exception: text on `--gold-bg` celeste band (always fixed `#fff` or `#000`, never `var(--fg)`). Every color in the JSON has dark/light variants—test both themes before claiming done.
- **Themes:** `[data-theme="light"]` on `<html>` swaps all colors automatically. Your job: ensure contrast is AA (4.5:1 body, 3:1 title) in BOTH dark and light.
- **Cards:** Reuse the catalog from nexcyber-design-system.md (§ Catálogo de cards). Do NOT invent new card types. If content doesn't fit an existing card, document the new type in nexcyber-design-system.md FIRST.
- **Mobile:** No :hover on touch. Provide keyboard/tap equivalent (toggle via click, or reveal by default ≤700px). Never hide content behind hover.

**STEP 3 — Document decisions in the same turn:**
- Color/component changes → nexcyber-design-system.md (add/update relevant section)
- New card type → add entry to § Catálogo de cards + describe structure, fondo, radius, uso
- New mobile breakpoint behavior → add row to § Comportamiento en mobile
- Component implementation notes → nexcyber-design-tokens.json llmImplementationNotes (if complex pattern)

## Celeste band implementation contract (§2, Nueva sección - guía de estructura.md)

Every top-level page alternates **celeste band / theme band** starting with celeste after the hero:
1. **Structure:** `background: var(--gold-bg)` + `::before` pseudo-element set to `var(--bg)` at `opacity: 0` + class `.band-lit` which sets that opacity to 0 when band enters viewport (via `.band-lit` state in CSS, managed by IntersectionObserver in `assets/main.js`).
2. **IntersectionObserver selector update:** When adding a new celeste band, append its class (`.why-band`, `.proc-band`, `.res-band`, `.p-band`, etc.) to the selector in `assets/main.js` (around line 140), otherwise the fade won't trigger.
3. **NEVER declare own background on direct children** of a celeste band — celeste must show through the veil. `.pil-card` inside `.why-band` does NOT get its own bg (exception: `.pil-card` is explicitly overridden in the original CSS, approved for this one case; document if adding others).
4. **Text on --gold-bg is ALWAYS fixed:** `#fff` or `#000`, never `var(--fg)` or `var(--fg-soft)`. This is the ONLY exception to "all color via variable" because `--gold-bg` is identical in both themes and needs correct contrast in both without variable fallback.

## Accessibility & visual hierarchy

**WCAG AA compliance (no exceptions):** 4.5:1 minimum for body text, 3:1 for headings, against their actual background (dark or light). Never use tonal subtlety (e.g., dimmed `--fg-soft` at low opacity) to lower visual weight. Instead, adjust `font-weight` or `font-size`. Modulate hierarchy with scale and weight, not color tone.

**Paragraph flow (no forced breaks):** No `<br>` inside body paragraphs (.lead, .p-body, .svc p, card descriptions). `<br>` only in titles/headlines where line break is a typography decision. All body paragraphs must include `text-wrap: pretty` to avoid orphaned words. `max-width` in `ch` **only in three places** (see nexcyber-design-system.md): hero lead, closing CTA band, footer. Everything else grows with its container.

## Code patterns

**Preserve existing vanilla JS:** `assets/main.js`, `assets/content.js`, per-page `.js` files. No React, JSX, or UI frameworks.

**No new libraries:** Existing (GSAP/ScrollTrigger) load with local fallback (`assets/vendor/README.txt`). No new CDN libraries without explicit request.

**No new visual styles:** All colors, typography, spacing, radii, shadows come from nexcyber-design-tokens.json. Use classes (`.h2`, `.lead`, `.eyebrow`, `.btn-primary`, `.section-pad`) or `var(--token)`, never hardcoded hex or px.

**Header/footer verbatim:** Never reinterpret their markup across pages—copy exactly.

**All visible text via data-i attribute:** `data-i="key"` in HTML + entry in `assets/content.js` (`NX_CONTENT[lang]`) for EN and ES. Never hardcode copy.

**Scroll reveals & band fade handled by main.js:** `[data-reveal]`, `[data-reveal-dir]`, `[data-reveal-head]` and `.band-lit` opacity already managed. Don't write custom animation CSS/JS.

**Test in dark and light, both languages, mobile ≤700px / ≤900px (see breakpoints in nexcyber-design-system.md § Comportamiento en mobile).**

## Deliverables / Export

When preparing a zip or deployment package, include ONLY production files and design context:

- All `.html` files
- `assets/` (CSS, JS, vendor libraries, fonts)
- `robots.txt`, `sitemap.xml`
- `docs/` (all guides, including content guides and design system)
- `CLAUDE.md`, `nexcybers.mdc`
- `Nexcybers Color Palette.md`
- `docs/design-system/nexcyber-design-tokens.json`
- `docs/design-system/nexcyber-design-system.md`

**ALWAYS EXCLUDE:** `screenshots/`, `uploads/`, `dist/` (verification captures, chat references, old builds—none are referenced by any page).

## Document maintenance (critical for AI consistency)

**Any new or changed design decision must be documented in the same turn it's made.** Not optional, not later. The code is implementation; the docs are the contract. Without documentation, the next AI agent invents inconsistently.

- **New color token or color change** → update `Nexcybers Color Palette.md` and `nexcyber-design-tokens.json`
- **New card type or variant** → add to `nexcyber-design-system.md` § Catálogo de cards before reuse
- **New spacing/sizing value** → verify it's a 4px multiple; document in `nexcyber-design-tokens.json` if it becomes a reusable token
- **New button variant or change** → document in `nexcyber-design-system.md` § Botones
- **New mobile breakpoint or responsive behavior** → add row to `nexcyber-design-system.md` § Comportamiento en mobile
- **New component pattern (visuals, motion, interaction)** → document in `nexcyber-design-tokens.json` llmImplementationNotes + reference in this `.mdc` if it's a constraint
- **New category tint or category logic** → update `nexcyber-design-system.md` § Category Tints

## AI Constraints (bind all agents)

- **Read design guides first.** No visual change without consulting nexcyber-design-tokens.json and nexcyber-design-system.md.
- **Never hardcode colors or spacing.** Always use CSS variables or classes from the catalog.
- **Spacing uses 4px multiples ONLY.** (4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 32, 40, 48, 56, 64…). Never 14px, 18px, 22px.
- **Typography class-driven.** .display, .h2, .h3, .lead for semantic meaning; never override font-size.
- **One button component, two variants.** .btn-primary and .btn-ghost only. Never invent a third.
- **Card catalog reuse.** Use existing cards (.trust-card, .svc, .rcard, .pil-card, .p-pair, .proc-band, .contact-info-card, etc.). Document new types in § Catálogo before reuse.
- **No variables on text over --gold-bg.** Fixed #fff or #000 only.
- **Test both dark and light themes.** Every color token has two values; both must work.
- **Mobile :hover equivalence.** If reveal/state is behind :hover on desktop, provide click toggle or show-by-default ≤700px on mobile.
- **No forced line breaks in paragraphs.** `<br>` only in titles. Body paragraphs carry `text-wrap: pretty`.
- **Band celeste contract:** background: var(--gold-bg) + ::before overlay + .band-lit class + IntersectionObserver hook. Never own background on children.
- **Document decisions in the same turn.** Not optional. Every visual change → corresponding guide entry.
